{% set local_problem %}
<p>Arab homes face a challenge that flat-land properties don't: gravity-concentrated water flow. When you're on Brindlee Mountain and it rains, water doesn't just fall on your roof — it flows downhill from above your property too. Your gutters need to handle more volume than the square footage of your roof might suggest.</p>

<p>Many older Arab homes still have original sectional gutters that are well past their effective lifespan. The seams have separated, debris has accumulated at every joint, and water cascades over the sides during moderate rain. On sloped terrain, that overflow heads straight toward your foundation at increased velocity.</p>

<p>Even newer Arab homes often have undersized gutters installed by builders focused on cost rather than performance. When those 5-inch sectional gutters meet a mountain thunderstorm, they simply can't keep up. Water backs up, overflows, and the resulting erosion and foundation damage costs far more than proper gutters would have.</p>

<p>Seamless gutters solve these problems. No seams means no leak points. Custom sizing means capacity matched to your roof. For Arab's mountain terrain, there's simply no better choice.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Seamless gutters are continuous gutters with no seams except at corners and downspout connections. Unlike sectional gutters made of pre-cut 10-foot sections joined together, seamless gutters are fabricated on-site from a single piece of aluminum coil — custom-cut to the exact length of each run on your home.</p>

<p>Why does this matter? Because seams are where gutters fail. Every joint in a sectional gutter system is a potential leak point, a place for debris to catch, and a weak spot that can separate over time. On Arab's hilly terrain, failed seams don't just drip — they channel water directly toward your foundation.</p>

<p>We bring our portable gutter machine directly to your Arab home, feed in aluminum coil, and fabricate your gutters right in your driveway. The result is a precision-fit gutter system designed specifically for your roofline — not generic sections that don't quite fit.</p>
{% endset %}

